      answer: "D",
      solution: `<p> (d)<br/> Number of ways to form one digit number = 2<br/> ‘0 ’cannot be treated as one digit number<br/> Number of ways to form two digit number = 2 ×3 = 6<br/> Number of ways to form three digit number = 2 ×3 ×3 = 18<br/> Number of ways to form four digit number = 2 ×3<sup>3</sup> = 54<br/> Number of ways to form five digit number = 2 ×3<sup>4</sup> = 162<br/> Number of ways to foron six digit number = 2 ×3<sup>5</sup> = 486<br/>Total number of ways = 2 + 6 + 18 + 54 + 162 + 486 = 728 </p>`,
